{
	"description": "The desktop's golden projection (phase 5 no-terminal amendment, 9.3; D168): one input, and what `loam deployment write --host desktop` (@lushly-dev/loam-cli's desktop-golden.test.ts) and loam-desktop's Rust materializer (step 9b) each write from it. `apps` is in the projection's order, which is the materializer's (plugin id, then app id); each names the plugin that brings it. An expected file's bytes are its object here, keys in the order written, serialized with tab indentation and a trailing newline. The mounted app lets its views render (`views`, D169), which the materializer reads from `engine.mount` and the CLI from the entry. `mounts` lists the fields both write; the CLI adds `bearer`, the materializer `bearer_keychain` and `proof_key`, which each test asserts apart. `variants` are further inputs, each the input above with its `patch` applied as an RFC 7386 JSON merge patch (null removes a key; an array is replaced whole), and what both write from it: the same input on Windows, whose sandbox origin differs; and a desktop with no view and no provider, so `frame-src 'none'`, whose engine authenticates nothing and leaves `labels` and `approvals` to their defaults, and mounts its app as an instance, `inbox`, whose id is not its package's, `mail`.",
